19:["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground","children":"Samadhi is the culmination of deep yogic concentration and meditation. It refers to complete absorption in the object of contemplation, and in its highest form, transcendence of the ordinary subject-object split. While often spoken of as mystical, it is also presented systematically in the yogic tradition as the matured fruit of ethics, discipline, concentration, and sustained meditative practice."}]
1a:["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground mt-4","children":"Samadhi is central to the Yoga Sutras and appears across Hindu and Buddhist contemplative traditions as the apex of meditative stabilization. In Vedantic interpretation, it supports or reveals direct knowledge of the Self."}]
